const e={id:"node-events-emitter",title:{en:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture"},difficulty:"Intermediate",readTime:9,sections:[{type:"concept",heading:{en:"1. What is the EventEmitter in Node.js?",hi:"1. Node.js Mein EventEmitter Kya Hota Hai?"},body:{en:"Node.js is fundamentally an **event-driven architecture**. Much of the Node core standard library is built directly on top of the **`EventEmitter`** class from the built-in **`node:events`** module.\n\nWhen you work with:\n- An HTTP server (`server.on('request', ...)`)\n- A readable stream (`stream.on('data', ...)`)\n- A WebSocket connection (`socket.on('message', ...)`)\n\n...you are using objects that inherit directly from `EventEmitter`!\n\n### The Observer / Pub-Sub Pattern\nThe `EventEmitter` implements the **Publish-Subscribe (Pub/Sub) pattern**:\n1. **The Publisher (Emitter)**: Emits a named string event when something happens (`emitter.emit('user:registered', userData)`).\n2. **The Subscribers (Listeners)**: One or more listener functions registered to that event execute whenever the event fires (`emitter.on('user:registered', sendWelcomeEmail)`).\n\nThe publisher does not know or care who is listening. This **decouples** your application logic!",hi:"Node.js ka poora architecture **Event-Driven** hota hai. Node core ki lagbhag saari badi libraries **`node:events`** module ke **`EventEmitter`** class par based hain.\n\nChahe aap:\n- HTTP server ka `server.on('request')` sunein\n- File stream ka `stream.on('data')` sunein\n- Ya socket ka `socket.on('message')` sunein\n\n...yeh sabhi objects internally `EventEmitter` ko hi inherit karte hain!\n\n### Observer / Pub-Sub Pattern Kya Hai?\n1. **Publisher (Event Emit Karne Wala)**: Jab koi action hota hai, toh yeh ek named event announce karta hai (`emitter.emit('order:created', orderData)`).\n2. **Subscribers (Listeners)**: Wo functions jo is event ko sunte hain aur apna-apna kaam karte hain (`emitter.on('order:created', sendSmsNotification)`).\n\nPublisher ko is baat se koi matlab nahi hota ki kaun-kaun use sun raha hai. Is pattern se hamara backend code clean aur **decoupled** rehta hai!"}},{type:"concept",heading:{en:"2. Why Event-Driven Architecture Matters in Backend Systems",hi:"2. Event-Driven Architecture Kyun Zaroori Hai?"},body:{en:`Imagine an e-commerce checkout function:
When a customer buys a laptop, you must:
1. Charge their credit card.
2. Send an email invoice.
3. Send an SMS confirmation.
4. Notify the warehouse packing system.
5. Track marketing analytics.

### Without EventEmitter (Tightly Coupled):
All 5 tasks are written inside one giant monolithic checkout function. If the SMS service fails, the entire payment checkout crashes!

### With EventEmitter (Cleanly Decoupled):
The checkout function charges the card and simply emits \`order:placed\`.
Separate micro-services or helper modules independently listen to \`order:placed\`. Adding a new feature (like loyalty reward points) requires zero changes to the original checkout controller!`,hi:`Sochiye kisi shopping app par customer ne order place kiya:
Ab aapko:
1. Payment charge karna hai.
2. Email invoice bhejna hai.
3. SMS bhejna hai.
4. Warehouse ko packing alert dena hai.
5. Analytics update karni hai.

### Bina EventEmitter Ke (Messy Code):
Saara code ek hi 200-line ke function mein likhna padega. Agar SMS bhejne mein error aayi, toh customer ka order checkout bhi crash ho jayega!

### EventEmitter Ke Saath (Decoupled & Clean):
Checkout function payment charge karke seedha \`emitter.emit('order:placed', order)\` announce kar deta hai.
Email service, SMS service aur Warehouse alag baithkar is event ko listen karte hain. Kal ko agar Naya Feature (jaise Scratch Card Reward) add karna ho, toh checkout function ko chhoone ki bhi zaroorat nahi padegi!`}},{type:"analogy",heading:{en:"Real-Life Analogy: The Railway Station Loudspeaker Announcement",hi:"Real-Life Analogy: Railway Station Ka Loudspeaker Announcement"},body:{en:`Consider an announcement at **New Delhi Railway Station**:

- **The Station Announcer (The EventEmitter)**: Speaks into the microphone:
  > *"Attention passengers! Train #12301 Rajdhani Express is arriving on Platform 4."*
  > \`station.emit('train:arrived', { trainNo: 12301, platform: 4 })\`
- **The Independent Listeners (\`.on()\` subscribers)**:
  - **Passengers** gather their suitcases and walk to Platform 4.
  - **Coolies / Porters** rush to Platform 4 with luggage trolleys.
  - **Chai Wallahs** start boiling fresh tea kettles.
  - **Ticket Examiners (TTE)** verify their passenger manifest charts.
- The station announcer does not personally walk up to each passenger or tea vendor. The announcer broadcasts the event once, and all interested parties act independently!`,hi:`Sochiye **New Delhi Railway Station** par loudspeaker announcement:

- **Station Announcer (EventEmitter)**: Mic par bolta hai:
  > *"Kripya dhyan dein, gaadi sankhya 12301 Rajdhani Express Platform number 4 par aa rahi hai."*
  > \`station.emit('train:arrival', { platform: 4 })\`
- **Sunne Wale Listeners (\`.on()\`):**
  - **Yatri** apna bag utha kar Platform 4 ki taraf badhte hain.
  - **Coolie** trolley lekar Platform 4 par daudte hain.
  - **Chai wale** jaldi se garam chai banana shuru karte hain.
  - **TTE** reservation chart check karte hain.
- Announcer kisi ke kaan mein jaakar personally nahi bolta. Usne bas ek baar announcement ki, aur sabhi logo ne apna-apna kaam independently kar liya!`}},{type:"syntax",heading:{en:"4. Syntax: Essential EventEmitter API Methods",hi:"4. Syntax: EventEmitter Ke Zaroori Methods"},body:{en:`\`\`\`javascript
import { EventEmitter } from 'node:events';

const emitter = new EventEmitter();

// 1. Subscribe to an event (runs every time the event fires)
emitter.on('event:name', (data) => {
  console.log('Received:', data);
});

// 2. Subscribe ONCE (runs only on the first trigger, then auto-unsubscribes)
emitter.once('user:first_login', () => {
  console.log('Welcome gift credited!');
});

// 3. Emit / Fire an event with payload data
emitter.emit('event:name', { id: 101, status: 'SUCCESS' });

// 4. Remove a specific listener
emitter.off('event:name', listenerFunction);

// 5. Default Max Listeners (10)
// If you add > 10 listeners to an event, Node logs a memory leak warning!
emitter.setMaxListeners(20);
\`\`\``,hi:`\`\`\`javascript
import { EventEmitter } from 'node:events';

const emitter = new EventEmitter();

// 1. Event Listen Karna (har baar chalega)
emitter.on('user:signup', (user) => {
  console.log('New user:', user.name);
});

// 2. Sirf 1 Baar Sunna (pehli baar chal kar automatically un-subscribe ho jayega)
emitter.once('app:ready', () => {
  console.log('Server initialized!');
});

// 3. Event Fire / Trigger Karna
emitter.emit('user:signup', { name: 'Aman', email: 'aman@test.com' });

// 4. Listener Hatana
emitter.off('user:signup', myListenerFunction);

// 5. Default Limit (10 Listeners)
// 10 se zyada listeners lagane par Node memory leak warning deta hai
emitter.setMaxListeners(25);
\`\`\``}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"5. Practical Examples: Order System, Class Extension & Error Handling",hi:"5. Practical Examples: E-Commerce System, Class Inheritance aur Error Events"},body:{en:`### Example 1: Basic Event Emission with Payload Arguments
Demonstrating multiple independent listeners subscribed to a single notification event.`,hi:`### Example 1: Basic Event Emission Aur Multiple Listeners
Dekhiye kaise ek single event par multiple independent functions trigger hote hain.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"basicEventEmitter.js",snippet:`// Example 1: Decoupled Order Event Hub
import { EventEmitter } from "node:events";

const orderHub = new EventEmitter();

// Listener 1: Email Notification Service
orderHub.on("order:placed", (order) => {
  console.log(\`📧 [Email Service]: Sending invoice receipt to \${order.customerEmail}\`);
});

// Listener 2: SMS Gateway Service
orderHub.on("order:placed", (order) => {
  console.log(\`📱 [SMS Gateway]: Alert sent for order #\${order.id} (Amount: ₹\${order.total})\`);
});

// Listener 3: One-time first order bonus coupon
orderHub.once("order:placed", (order) => {
  console.log(\`🎁 [Promotions]: First order recorded! Credited 100 reward points.\`);
});

// Simulating Order Placement
console.log("Processing Order 1...");
orderHub.emit("order:placed", { id: "ORD_101", total: 4999, customerEmail: "priya@example.com" });

console.log("\\nProcessing Order 2...");
// Notice the once() listener will NOT run for Order 2!
orderHub.emit("order:placed", { id: "ORD_102", total: 1299, customerEmail: "rahul@example.com" });`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 2: Custom Class Extending EventEmitter",hi:"Example 2: EventEmitter Ko Extend Karke Custom Class Banana"},body:{en:`### Example 2: Building an Event-Driven Stock Ticker
Creating an enterprise class that emits pricing events as real-time market values fluctuate.`,hi:"### Example 2: Real-World Stock Price Ticker Class\nClasses mein `extends EventEmitter` karke real-time events broadcast karne ka standard pattern."},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"stockTicker.js",snippet:`// Example 2: Custom Domain Class extending EventEmitter
import { EventEmitter } from "node:events";

class StockTicker extends EventEmitter {
  constructor(symbol, initialPrice) {
    super(); // Always invoke super() constructor!
    this.symbol = symbol;
    this.price = initialPrice;
  }

  updatePrice(newPrice) {
    const oldPrice = this.price;
    this.price = newPrice;
    const change = ((newPrice - oldPrice) / oldPrice) * 100;

    // Emit price update event with detailed statistics
    this.emit("price:change", {
      symbol: this.symbol,
      oldPrice,
      newPrice,
      percentChange: change.toFixed(2)
    });

    if (newPrice > 3000) {
      this.emit("alert:allTimeHigh", { symbol: this.symbol, price: newPrice });
    }
  }
}

// Instantiating the stock ticker
const reliance = new StockTicker("RELIANCE", 2850);

// Subscribing to price updates
reliance.on("price:change", (data) => {
  console.log(\`📈 [\${data.symbol}]: ₹\${data.oldPrice} -> ₹\${data.newPrice} (\${data.percentChange}%)\`);
});

reliance.on("alert:allTimeHigh", (data) => {
  console.log(\`🚨 BREAKING ALERT: \${data.symbol} hit all-time high of ₹\${data.price}!\`);
});

reliance.updatePrice(2920);
reliance.updatePrice(3050);`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 3: Mandatory 'error' Event Handling in Node.js",hi:"Example 3: 'error' Event Ka Mandatory Rule Aur App Crash Se Bachna"},body:{en:"### Example 3: The Special 'error' Event Rule\nIn Node.js, if an EventEmitter emits an `'error'` event and there is **no listener registered for 'error'**, Node treats it as an unhandled exception and immediately crashes the process!",hi:`### Example 3: Node.js Ka Special 'error' Event
Agar kisi EventEmitter par 'error' event emit ho aur koi listener na ho, toh Node.js poore server process ko crash kar deta hai. Isliye 'error' listener hamesha lagana zaroori hota hai.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"errorEventHandling.js",snippet:`// Example 3: Proper error event handling
import { EventEmitter } from "node:events";

class PaymentGateway extends EventEmitter {
  processTransaction(cardDetails) {
    if (!cardDetails.cvv) {
      // Emitting an 'error' event
      this.emit("error", new Error("Invalid payment payload: CVV missing"));
      return;
    }
    this.emit("success", { txnId: "TXN_8849" });
  }
}

const payment = new PaymentGateway();

// CRITICAL: Always attach an 'error' listener!
payment.on("error", (err) => {
  console.error(\`🛡️ [Caught Payment Error Safely]: \${err.message}\`);
});

payment.on("success", (res) => {
  console.log("Payment successful! Txn:", res.txnId);
});

// Triggering failure (handled gracefully without crashing process!)
payment.processTransaction({ cardNumber: "4111222233334444" });`}},{type:"mistakes",heading:{en:"6. Common Mistakes with EventEmitters",hi:"6. EventEmitters Mein Hone Wali Badi Galtiyan"},mistakes:[{mistake:{en:"Memory Leaks by repeatedly registering listeners inside request handlers (MaxListenersExceededWarning).",hi:"Har incoming request ke andar naya listener register karna jisse Memory Leak ho jata hai."},correction:{en:"Never call `emitter.on()` inside an Express request handler unless you clean it up with `emitter.off()`. Re-registering listeners on every HTTP request leaks memory and triggers the 10-listener warning.",hi:"Express route handler ke andar `emitter.on()` na likhein. Server start hote waqt listeners ko sirf ek baar bind karein."},code:`// DISASTROUS ANTI-PATTERN:
app.get('/order', (req, res) => {
  // Registers a NEW listener on every single GET request!
  // At request #11, Node prints MaxListenersExceededWarning!
  eventHub.on('order', () => {}); 
});`},{mistake:{en:"Using an anonymous arrow function with `emitter.off(event, () => {})`.",hi:"`emitter.off()` mein anonymous arrow function pass karna."},correction:{en:"Every arrow function creates a new reference in memory. `emitter.off()` requires the exact reference to the original function to remove it from the listener array.",hi:"`emitter.off()` ko un-subscribe karne ke liye original function ka exact reference chahiye hota hai."},code:`// FAILS: Does NOT remove the listener!
emitter.on('data', () => console.log('hello'));
emitter.off('data', () => console.log('hello')); // Different memory reference!

// WORKS:
const onData = () => console.log('hello');
emitter.on('data', onData);
emitter.off('data', onData); // Successfully removed!`}]},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"7. Production Best Practices for Event Architecture",hi:"7. Event Architecture Ke Best Practices"},body:{en:"- **Always Listen to the 'error' Event**: Any class extending EventEmitter must have an `emitter.on('error', ...)` listener to prevent unexpected unhandled process termination.\n- **Use `.once()` for Temporary Subscriptions**: When waiting for a single lifecycle milestone (e.g. `db.once('open')`), always use `.once()` so the listener automatically unbinds.\n- **Synchronous Execution Caveat**: Remember that `EventEmitter.emit()` invokes all registered listeners **synchronously** in the order they were registered! To make listeners async, wrap listener bodies in `setImmediate` or use `events.on` async iterators.",hi:"- **'error' Event Hamesha Listen Karein**: Bina error listener ke emit hua error poore server ko crash kar deta hai.\n- **One-time Ke Liye `.once()` Use Karein**: Database connect hone jaisi one-time events ke liye `.once('open')` use karein taaki wo automatically unbind ho jaye.\n- **Listeners Synchronously Chalte Hain**: Dhyan rahe ki `emitter.emit()` listeners ko line se synchronous call karta hai. Agar unhe background mein bhejna ho toh listener ke andar `setImmediate()` lagayein."}},{type:"interview",heading:{en:"8. Top Interview Questions & Answers",hi:"8. Top Interview Sawal Aur Jawab"},questions:[{q:{en:"What happens if an EventEmitter emits an 'error' event and no listener is attached?",hi:"Agar EventEmitter par 'error' event emit ho aur koi listener na ho toh kya hota hai?"},a:{en:"Node.js treats unhandled 'error' events as a special case. It prints a full stack trace, throws an uncaught exception, and abruptly crashes the entire Node.js runtime process with exit code 1. Therefore, robust applications must always register at least one 'error' event handler.",hi:"Node.js unhandled 'error' events ko fatal maanta hai. Stack trace print hota hai, uncaught exception throw hoti hai aur poora Node.js process exit code 1 ke saath crash ho jata hai. Isliye 'error' listener lagana anivarya hota hai."}},{q:{en:"Are EventEmitter listeners executed synchronously or asynchronously by default?",hi:"EventEmitter ke listeners default mein synchronously execute hote hain ya asynchronously?"},a:{en:"Synchronously! When `emitter.emit('event')` is called, the EventEmitter iterates through its internal array of registered listener functions and calls each one synchronously on the Call Stack in the exact order they were registered. Control does not return past the `emit()` line until all synchronous listeners finish executing.",hi:"Synchronously! Jab `emitter.emit()` call hota hai, toh wo apne saare registered listeners ko usi waqt ek ke baad ek Call Stack par synchronously execute karta hai. Jab tak saare listeners execute nahi ho jaate, emit() ke aage ki line execute nahi hoti."}},{q:{en:"Why does Node.js log a `MaxListenersExceededWarning` when you add more than 10 listeners?",hi:"10 se zyada listeners add karne par Node.js `MaxListenersExceededWarning` kyun deta hai?"},a:{en:"The default limit of 10 listeners is a built-in safety net designed to help developers identify accidental memory leaks (such as binding an event listener inside a recurring loop or request handler). If an event genuinely requires more than 10 legitimate subscribers, the limit can be safely increased using `emitter.setMaxListeners(n)`.",hi:"10 listeners ki default limit ek safety feature hai jo developers ko memory leaks pakadne mein madad karti hai (jaise kisi loop ke andar bar-bar listener add ho jana). Agar sach mein 10 se zyada listeners ki zaroorat ho, toh `emitter.setMaxListeners(number)` se limit badhayi ja sakti hai."}}]},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"9. Summary Cheatsheet",hi:"9. Summary Cheatsheet"},body:{en:"- **EventEmitter**: Heart of Node's event-driven architecture (`node:events`).\n- **.on()**: Persistent listener for repeated events.\n- **.once()**: Fires once and self-destructs.\n- **.emit()**: Synchronously invokes all registered listeners.\n- **Critical Rule**: Always handle the `'error'` event.",hi:`- **EventEmitter**: Node ka core Pub/Sub system.
- **.on()**: Baar-baar trigger hone wale events ke liye.
- **.once()**: Sirf 1 baar chalne ke liye.
- **.emit()**: Event fire karta hai (synchronous execution).
- **Rule**: 'error' event ka listener lagana zaroori hai.`}}],quiz:[{q:{en:"What happens if an 'error' event is emitted on an EventEmitter instance that has NO listeners registered for 'error'?",hi:"Agar kisi EventEmitter par 'error' event emit ho aur koi listener na ho toh kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Node.js crashes the entire process with an uncaught exception",hi:"Node.js uncaught exception ke saath poora process crash kar deta hai"},{en:"It prints a soft console warning and continues running",hi:"Yeh sirf console warning print karta hai aur chalta rehta hai"},{en:"The error is silently ignored",hi:"Error silently ignore ho jata hai"},{en:"It retries the operation 3 times",hi:"Yeh operation 3 baar retry karta hai"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"Unhandled error events in Node.js are treated as fatal errors that throw an uncaught exception, terminating the process.",hi:"Node.js unhandled error event ko fatal manta hai aur crash kar deta hai."}},{q:{en:"What is the default maximum number of listeners that can be attached to an event before Node prints a memory leak warning?",hi:"Memory leak warning aane se pehle kisi event par default mein maximum kitne listeners attach kiye ja sakte hain?"},options:[{en:"10",hi:"10"},{en:"100",hi:"100"},{en:"5",hi:"5"},{en:"Unlimited",hi:"Unlimited"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"By default, Node sets a threshold of 10 listeners per event to catch memory leaks early.",hi:"Default threshold 10 listeners hota hai taaki memory leaks ko shuru mein hi pakda ja sake."}},{q:{en:"How are listener functions executed when `emitter.emit()` is called?",hi:"`emitter.emit()` call hone par listener functions kaise execute hote hain?"},options:[{en:"Synchronously in the order they were registered",hi:"Synchronously, usi order mein jis order mein register hue the"},{en:"Asynchronously on the Macrotask Queue",hi:"Asynchronously Macrotask Queue par"},{en:"In reverse alphabetical order",hi:"Ulte alphabetical order mein"},{en:"In separate OS worker threads",hi:"Alag-alag OS worker threads par"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"EventEmitter calls all registered listeners synchronously on the current Call Stack.",hi:"EventEmitter saare listeners ko usi waqt synchronously Call Stack par execute karta hai."}},{question:{en:"What is the core architectural purpose of EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture in the modern full-stack MERN ecosystem?",hi:"Modern full-stack MERN ecosystem mein EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ka mukhya architectural maksad kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"It manages physical computer cooling and power supply",hi:"Ye physical computer cooling aur power supply manage karta hai"},{en:"It provides structured, robust, and scalable patterns for handling eventemitter & event-driven architecture with high performance and maintainability",hi:"Ye high performance aur maintainability ke saath EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ko handle karne ka structured aur scalable pattern provide karta hai"},{en:"It completely replaces JavaScript with binary machine code in browser tabs",hi:"Ye browser tabs mein JavaScript ko binary machine code se replace karta hai"},{en:"It is only used for printing documents to physical printers",hi:"Ye sirf physical printers par documents print karne ke liye hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture establishes clean separation of concerns, ensuring predictable data flow, robust error handling, and optimal runtime performance in production.",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture clean architecture aur separation of concerns deta hai jisse application scalable aur maintainable banti hai."}},{question:{en:"What critical development bottleneck or anti-pattern does EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture directly resolve?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture kis critical development bottleneck ya anti-pattern ko seedhe solve karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It replaces chaotic, tightly coupled ad-hoc logic with declarative, predictable control flow and structured data contracts",hi:"Ye chaotic aur tightly coupled logic ko hata kar declarative, predictable flow aur structured data contracts deta hai"},{en:"It forces the operating system to shut down when errors occur",hi:"Error aane par ye operating system band kar deta hai"},{en:"It deletes all database records older than 24 hours automatically",hi:"Ye 24 ghante purane DB records delete karta hai"},{en:"It blocks all outgoing HTTP network requests to conserve bandwidth",hi:"Ye bandwidth bachane ke liye network requests block karta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Without EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture, applications suffer from brittle code, maintenance overhead, and unhandled edge cases that manifest as production crashes.",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ke bina code brittle ho jata hai aur production mein unexpected errors aate hain."}},{question:{en:"When reasoning about EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture, how is its mental model best conceptualized through real-world analogies?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ko real-world analogies ke zariye kaise best samjha ja sakta hai?"},options:[{en:"As a completely offline computer with zero network or database connections",hi:"Ek offline computer ki tarah jisme koi connection na ho"},{en:"As a disciplined, coordinated workflow where inputs are validated and processed through standardized checkpoints rather than ad-hoc handling",hi:"Ek disciplined workflow ki tarah jahan data ko structured checkpoints ke zariye step-by-step process kiya jata hai"},{en:"As a random number generator with non-deterministic output",hi:"Random number generator ki tarah jiska koi niyam na ho"},{en:"As a static text document that cannot be modified or read",hi:"Static text document jo padha na ja sake"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Real-world workflow analogies help engineers visualize component boundaries, request lifecycles, and data transformations intuitively.",hi:"Real-world analogies component boundaries aur request lifecycle ko visual aur intuitive banati hain."}},{question:{en:"When declaring and implementing EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture, what syntactic convention is essential to prevent runtime errors?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ko declare aur implement karte waqt kaunsa syntax niyam runtime errors rokne ke liye zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Adhering strictly to required parameters, handling asynchronous promises/callbacks cleanly, and verifying return value types",hi:"Zaroori parameters sahi pass karna, async promises ko handle karna aur return value types verify karna"},{en:"Wrapping every line of code inside an eval() execution block",hi:"Har line ko eval() block mein wrap karna"},{en:"Omitting import and require statements to reduce file size",hi:"File size ghatane ke liye import statements hatana"},{en:"Writing all code on a single continuous line without whitespace",hi:"Bina whitespace ke single line par code likhna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Following standard ES6+ syntax contracts and properly handling promise resolution ensures execution safety and eliminates TypeError exceptions.",hi:"ES6+ syntax aur promise handling ke standard rules follow karne se TypeError aur crashes nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"What is a common pitfall developers encounter when working with EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ke saath kaam karte waqt developers aksar kaunsi aam galati karte hain?"},options:[{en:"Writing unit tests before implementing features",hi:"Feature likhne se pehle unit tests likhna"},{en:"Failing to handle failure edge cases, mutating shared state directly, or neglecting defensive validation guard clauses",hi:"Failure edge cases ko handle na karna, shared state direct mutate karna ya validation guard clauses na lagana"},{en:"Using strict equality checks (===) instead of loose equality (==)",hi:"Loose equality ke badle strict equality use karna"},{en:"Writing clear inline code documentation",hi:"Clear inline code comments likhna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Neglecting edge cases and error handling causes silent regressions and race conditions that surface under concurrent user workloads.",hi:"Edge cases aur error handling miss karne se high-traffic production load mein silent bugs paida hote hain."}},{question:{en:"According to production best practices, how should EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture be architected for enterprise-grade stability?",hi:"Production best practices ke mutabiq enterprise-grade stability ke liye EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ko kaise architect karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Enforce modular boundaries, validate all incoming payloads against schemas, log structured context, and maintain pure functions where possible",hi:"Modular boundaries enforce karein, payloads ko schema se validate karein, structured logs rakhein aur pure functions use karein"},{en:"Hardcode sensitive database connection strings directly in client-side files",hi:"Database passwords ko client files mein hardcode karna"},{en:"Disable all linter rules and type warnings globally",hi:"Linter aur type warnings ko globally disable karna"},{en:"Store all user session variables in global un-scoped memory arrays",hi:"Global memory arrays mein sessions store karna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Enterprise-grade code prioritizes modularity, strict input validation, structured observability, and stateless designs.",hi:"Production hardening ke liye modular code, schema validation aur observability standard rules hote hain."}},{question:{en:"How does proper optimization of EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture impact application memory and CPU consumption?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ko sahi dhang se optimize karne par application memory aur CPU par kya asar padta hai?"},options:[{en:"It increases server CPU temperature to 100 degrees Celsius",hi:"Server CPU temperature 100 degrees kar deta hai"},{en:"It minimizes redundant computations, eliminates memory leaks from uncleaned references, and maintains low latency under high concurrency",hi:"Ye redundant computations ghatata hai, memory leaks khatam karta hai aur high concurrency mein low latency maintain karta hai"},{en:"It doubles heap RAM allocation unconditionally",hi:"Heap RAM ko zabardasti double karta hai"},{en:"Optimization has zero measurable impact in modern web engines",hi:"Modern web engines par optimization ka koi asar nahi hota"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Preventing unnecessary allocations and cleaning up resources ensures low garbage collection pressure and predictable response times.",hi:"Memory leak rokne aur unnecessary allocations hatane se Garbage Collector par load kam rehta hai aur response fast rehta hai."}},{question:{en:"What security principle is non-negotiable when handling data within EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture mein data handle karte waqt kaunsa security principle non-negotiable hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Never trust client-supplied input: always sanitize, authenticate, authorize, and validate against strict schemas on the server",hi:"Client data par blind trust na karein: server par hamesha sanitize, authenticate, authorize aur validate karein"},{en:"Trust all requests coming from mobile devices or web browsers blindly",hi:"Mobile ya browser se aane wali requests par blind trust karein"},{en:"Disable HTTPS and SSL certificates to maximize raw network throughput",hi:"Network throughput ke liye HTTPS band karein"},{en:"Expose database admin credentials to all registered users",hi:"Database admin credentials sabhi users ko expose karein"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Zero-Trust security dictates that every incoming request and data mutation must be validated and authenticated server-side before processing.",hi:"Zero-Trust security ke mutabiq har incoming mutation ko server par strictly validate aur authenticate kiya jana chahiye."}},{question:{en:"How does asynchronous non-blocking execution operate in EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture mein asynchronous non-blocking execution kaise kaam karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It freezes the entire operating system until each operation completes",hi:"Har operation complete hone tak operating system freeze rehta hai"},{en:"I/O operations return Promises or accept callbacks, delegating work to background threads/queues while the main thread remains free to handle incoming tasks",hi:"I/O operations Promises return karte hain aur background queues use karke main thread ko baaki requests ke liye free rakhte hain"},{en:"Async operations execute in reverse alphabetical order automatically",hi:"Async operations reverse alphabetical order mein chalte hain"},{en:"Async code only executes when triggered manually by a user click",hi:"Sirf manual user click par async code chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Non-blocking asynchronous operations resolve via microtasks or event loop queues, ensuring the runtime thread serves concurrent requests smoothly.",hi:"Non-blocking model main thread ko free rakhta hai taaki server bina rukaawat ke multiple users ko simultaneously serve kar sake."}},{question:{en:"What is the recommended pattern for propagating errors that occur in EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture mein error aane par unhe propagate karne ka recommended pattern kya hai?"},options:[{en:"Intercepting the error, enriching it with operational context, and delegating to a centralized error handler or error boundary",hi:"Error ko intercept karna, debug context add karna, aur centralized error handler ya error boundary ko pass karna"},{en:"Swallowing errors silently with empty catch {} blocks to hide problems from logs",hi:"Khaali catch {} blocks se errors ko silently daba dena taaki logs mein na dikhein"},{en:"Shutting down the server machine power immediately",hi:"Server machine power turant band kar dena"},{en:"Sending internal raw stack traces and database credentials to end-user browsers",hi:"Raw stack trace aur DB passwords browser par bhej dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Centralized error propagation provides complete operational observability while shielding internal infrastructure details from end users.",hi:"Centralized error handling se system mein transparency rehti hai aur user ko clean, safe error messages milte hain."}},{question:{en:"When authoring unit or integration tests for EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture, what must the test suite assert?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ke liye automated tests likhte waqt test suite ko kya assert karna zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Only that the JavaScript file can be saved to disk",hi:"Sirf ye ki file disk par save ho sake"},{en:"Both the happy path (expected inputs producing valid outputs) AND boundary edge cases (null, empty arrays, network timeouts, invalid types)",hi:"Happy path (valid data) AUR boundary edge cases (null, empty array, network timeout, invalid types) dono ko verify karna"},{en:"That the test suite takes at least 24 hours to finish running",hi:"Test suite ko 24 ghante chalna chahiye"},{en:"Testing is considered unnecessary in modern full-stack development",hi:"Modern development mein testing zaroori nahi hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Robust automated test suites verify both standard valid scenarios and defensive failure modes to prevent regressions during deployments.",hi:"Achhi testing valid inputs aur failure states dono ko assert karti hai taaki production deployments safe rahein."}},{question:{en:"How does modular design enhance code maintainability in EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture?",hi:"Modular design EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture mein code maintainability ko kaise badhata hai?"},options:[{en:"By isolating distinct responsibilities into small, reusable, and independently testable units following the Single Responsibility Principle",hi:"Single Responsibility Principle ke zariye alag-alag kaamo ko chote, reusable aur testable units mein baant kar"},{en:"By combining all frontend, backend, and database code into a single 50,000-line script",hi:"Saara code ek hi 50,000-line script mein daal kar"},{en:"By removing all function names and replacing them with random numbers",hi:"Function names hata kar random numbers likhna"},{en:"By forbidding code comments and documentation across the repository",hi:"Comments aur documentation ban kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Modularity reduces cognitive load, simplifies debugging, prevents ripple effects during changes, and enables seamless team collaboration.",hi:"Modular code se readability badhti hai, debugging aasan hoti hai aur ek jagah badlav karne par doosri jagah bugs nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"When application traffic scales 100x, how should EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture be architected to support horizontal scaling?",hi:"Traffic 100x badhne par EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ko horizontally scale karne ke liye kya design approach honi chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Ensure the component/service is completely stateless, offload shared session/state to Redis/MongoDB, and distribute traffic via a load balancer",hi:"Service ko completely stateless banayein, shared state ko Redis/DB par shift karein aur load balancer se traffic distribute karein"},{en:"Store all user session variables in local in-memory JavaScript objects on the web server",hi:"Server ki local RAM mein session variables store karna"},{en:"Reboot the production server manually whenever memory usage exceeds 10%",hi:"Memory 10% cross hote hi server manually reboot karna"},{en:"Block 95% of incoming users using firewall rules",hi:"95% users ko firewall se block kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Stateless service architecture guarantees that any container instance can handle any incoming request, enabling dynamic auto-scaling without session loss.",hi:"Stateless architecture auto-scaling ka base hai jahan naye containers bina session loss ke instant traffic handle kar sakte hain."}},{question:{en:"In the full-stack MERN paradigm, where does EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture properly belong and execute?",hi:"Full-stack MERN architecture mein EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture kahan belong karta hai aur kahan execute hota hai?"},options:[{en:"In its designated architectural tier (Client browser UI, Express API backend, or MongoDB database) with clean API contracts connecting them",hi:"Apne designated tier (Browser UI, Express API backend, ya MongoDB) mein clean API contracts ke saath"},{en:"Directly on the end-user's local router firmware",hi:"User ke local router firmware par"},{en:"Inside the computer motherboard BIOS chip",hi:"Motherboard BIOS chip mein"},{en:"All MERN code runs strictly inside the MongoDB database engine",hi:"Saara MERN code sirf MongoDB ke andar chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Maintaining clear structural boundaries between client rendering, backend orchestration, and database persistence is the defining trait of MERN.",hi:"Client UI, backend server aur database ke beech saaf boundary maintain karna MERN architecture ka mukhya niyam hai."}},{question:{en:"What telemetry metric or observability signal is most crucial for diagnosing issues with EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture in production?",hi:"Production mein EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ki problems diagnose karne ke liye sabse zaroori telemetry metric kaunsi hoti hai?"},options:[{en:"The desktop monitor brightness setting of the client",hi:"Client ke monitor ki brightness"},{en:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (HTTP 4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), and heap memory allocation deltas",hi:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), aur heap memory allocation deltas"},{en:"The number of files in the project's root folder",hi:"Root folder mein files ki sankhya"},{en:"The physical keyboard model used by the engineer",hi:"Engineer ke keyboard ka model"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Observability platforms monitor p95/p99 latencies, error frequencies, and memory utilization to identify bottlenecks and regressions early.",hi:"p95/p99 latencies aur error rates monitor karne se crashes aane se pehle hi bottlenecks pakad mein aa jaate hain."}},{question:{en:"Why is eliminating unintended side effects essential when authoring logic for EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture ka logic likhte waqt unintended side effects ko khatam karna kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Side effects introduce unpredictability, corrupt shared state, cause race conditions, and make concurrent code nearly impossible to debug",hi:"Side effects se code unpredictable banta hai, shared state corrupt hoti hai aur race conditions create hoti hain"},{en:"Side effects permanently erase the developer's Git commit history",hi:"Git history permanently delete ho jaati hai"},{en:"Side effects are strictly required by the JavaScript ECMAScript standard",hi:"ECMAScript mein side effects required hain"},{en:"Side effects make all algorithms execute in O(1) time",hi:"Saare algorithms O(1) time mein chalte hain"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Pure and predictable logic produces the same output for identical inputs, guaranteeing thread safety, easy caching, and high reliability.",hi:"Pure logic se shared state safe rehti hai aur same input par hamesha consistent aur predictable output milta hai."}},{question:{en:"How should client-side state be kept in sync with backend server mutations in EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture mein client-side state aur backend server data ko sync mein kaise rakha jata hai?"},options:[{en:"By forcing a complete hard page refresh every 3 seconds",hi:"Har 3 second mein poora page hard refresh karke"},{en:"Using optimistic UI updates with error rollback, automated query cache invalidation (TanStack Query/RTK), or WebSocket change streams",hi:"Optimistic UI updates with rollback, automated query cache invalidation ya WebSocket push streams use karke"},{en:"By disabling all database update operations permanently",hi:"Database updates ko permanently band karke"},{en:"By saving user state in local CSV files on the server desktop",hi:"Server desktop par CSV files save karke"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Modern full-stack architectures synchronize state seamlessly using query cache invalidation, optimistic updates, and real-time socket events.",hi:"Modern apps cache invalidation aur optimistic UI use karti hain taaki UI bina screen reload ke instantly updated rahe."}},{question:{en:"Why is thorough resource cleanup (clearing timers, closing sockets, aborting in-flight requests) critical in EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture?",hi:"EventEmitter & Event-Driven Architecture mein resource cleanup (timers clear karna, sockets band karna, network abort karna) kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"To prevent memory leaks where unreachable or orphaned objects remain retained in heap memory, causing gradual performance degradation and crashes",hi:"Memory leaks rokne ke liye taaki unneeded objects RAM mein jama na hon aur server crash na ho"},{en:"To delete the client's local disk partition",hi:"Client ka local disk partition delete karne ke liye"},{en:"Because JavaScript engines allow only 5 variables in RAM",hi:"JS engine sirf 5 variables allow karta hai"},{en:"Cleanup is unnecessary because garbage collection handles 100% of event listeners automatically",hi:"Cleanup ki zaroorat nahi hoti"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Unclosed connections and dangling event listeners create references that prevent garbage collection, leading to severe memory leaks over time.",hi:"Dangling listeners aur unclosed connections memory leaks banate hain jo V8 heap ko exhaust karke process crash kar dete hain."}}]};export{e as default};
